# PARITY -- the engine libs arsenal copies from the fort are enforced
# byte-identical by libparity() (build.sh, run in ./build.sh ci). p3 cannot
# source the signed fort, so lib/cards lib/coach lib/ctx lib/grade lib/ui are
# duplicated by hand; a shared basename with NO row here MUST match its
# learn/lib namesake -- that default is what would have caught the two dropped
# ui fixes and the missing SRS callers before they shipped.
#
# a row records a REVIEWED, permanent divergence. it pins BOTH sides' current
# bytes, so the gate cannot be silenced by editing one file to match the other,
# or by editing both without re-pinning (either forces a visible diff a reviewer
# sees). regenerate a pair with:  sha256sum < learn/lib/X ; sha256sum < arsenal/lib/X
#
# path       side     sha256                                                            reason
lib/grade    learn    78cba52131d7dc086c121b5d86a35f3faa31727b4daa3bcffd1e5e0060a0881f  arsenal's run_answer/sandbox target lib/jail not the fort's nobody-sandbox; _answer_walk/answer_cmds/answer_flags are ported down from learn/learn (arsenal's thin driver has no call site). permanent, by design.
lib/grade    arsenal  687c978f293f1715f7cbffdbd54e9a9efd0baaa99a04f09887e9e739aa7a7481  (see the learn row) -- the arsenal-side copy of the same reviewed divergence.
